{"title":"2025 SSMO Speed Round Problems/Problem 10","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_SSMO_Speed_Round_Problems/Problem_10&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/f/36f73fc1312ee0349b3f3a0f3bd9eb5504339011.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> be a quadratic with a positive leading coefficient, and let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/5/b55ca7a0aa88ab7d58f4fc035317fdac39b17861.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> be a real number satisfying <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/7/5/e75989d4285e1953a1dfdd15e3d131ebb6cb2d8e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r &lt; 1 &lt; \\tfrac{5}{2r} &lt; 5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -7px\" width=\"119\" height=\"23\" />. Given that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/1/5/51553842162e03006f1b6def727c3032f10c3f17.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p(p(x)) = x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"93\" height=\"20\" /> for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/6/0162e0636d6af9bf59272aab703806aaa96eb19c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x \\in \\{ r,1,  \\tfrac{5}{2r} , 5\\}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -7px\" width=\"120\" height=\"23\" />, find <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/2/7/b2728900a565ef4ae77af001a499ff5ece3da0f9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p(12)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"43\" height=\"20\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_SSMO_Speed_Round_Problems/Problem_10&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Note that any fixed point of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/7/5/2751d79d3bbfb34440d68c685fe6ba7414951749.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p(x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"33\" height=\"18\" /> is also a fixed point of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/b/c/2bcd275befb5415ea6bd4c82e886e7515bda2ab9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p(p(x))$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"56\" height=\"18\" />. From the condition that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/1/5/51553842162e03006f1b6def727c3032f10c3f17.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p(p(x)) = x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"93\" height=\"20\" /> for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/2/2/522afe19d9ab0cbb84892b848ef1376f179258d8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x\\in \\{r,1,\\tfrac{5}{2r},5\\}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -7px\" width=\"120\" height=\"23\" />, we can conclude two things:\n</p>\n<ul>\n<li>The fixed points of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/f/36f73fc1312ee0349b3f3a0f3bd9eb5504339011.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> are a subset of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/6/c/16c4e29aecbc3c23cde06e84f9c99f5b596b8afd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\{r,1,\\tfrac{5}{2r},5\\}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -7px\" width=\"87\" height=\"23\" />;</li>\n<li><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/f/36f73fc1312ee0349b3f3a0f3bd9eb5504339011.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> has <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/1/bc1f9d9bf8a1b606a4188b5ce9a2af1809e27a89.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> fixed points.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>The main claim is that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/f/36f73fc1312ee0349b3f3a0f3bd9eb5504339011.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> has exactly <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> fixed points, and that these fixed points are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/0/79069377f91364c2f87a64e5f9f562a091c8a6c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p>First, we prove that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/f/36f73fc1312ee0349b3f3a0f3bd9eb5504339011.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> has exactly two fixed points. It is impossible that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/f/36f73fc1312ee0349b3f3a0f3bd9eb5504339011.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> has <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> fixed points because that would imply <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/4/b/e4bd3300ff31a2ab361552d72c5558c7af409996.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\deg p \\ge 4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"75\" height=\"18\" />. It is also impossible that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/f/36f73fc1312ee0349b3f3a0f3bd9eb5504339011.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> has <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/1/bc1f9d9bf8a1b606a4188b5ce9a2af1809e27a89.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> fixed points. For the sake of contradiction, suppose that this is the case. Then, the parabola <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/d/1/3d1db541df4771c9ef32bf4a78b920414c112e16.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y=p(x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"66\" height=\"18\" /> does not intersect the line <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/4/1/741a74d86df899c10724dc2f80638f5e7f599194.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y=x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"46\" height=\"13\" />, and since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/f/36f73fc1312ee0349b3f3a0f3bd9eb5504339011.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> has a positive leading coefficient, the parabola <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/d/1/3d1db541df4771c9ef32bf4a78b920414c112e16.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y=p(x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"66\" height=\"18\" /> lies entirely above the line <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/4/1/741a74d86df899c10724dc2f80638f5e7f599194.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y=x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"46\" height=\"13\" />. Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/f/36f73fc1312ee0349b3f3a0f3bd9eb5504339011.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> has no fixed points, the points <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/a/2/4a2695dcea82cf154dbfb0f95077f726c532d356.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(1, p(1))$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"66\" height=\"20\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/9/8/b98d295d171f68138ab41aa0e3054bc6b5d67a0e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(p(1), p(p(1))) = (p(1),1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"200\" height=\"20\" /> are distinct and lie on opposite sides of the line <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/4/1/741a74d86df899c10724dc2f80638f5e7f599194.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y=x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"46\" height=\"13\" />. However, both of these points lie on the parabola <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/d/1/3d1db541df4771c9ef32bf4a78b920414c112e16.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y=p(x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"66\" height=\"18\" />, which is a contradiction. Thus, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/f/36f73fc1312ee0349b3f3a0f3bd9eb5504339011.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> has exactly <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> fixed points.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/5/3/2532c85509f76b66eae6edfb538532c2e7d02f59.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] unitsize(0.27cm);  import contour; real f(real x, real y) { return 0.3x^2-y; } guide[][] thegraphs = contour(f, a=(-20,-20), b=(20,20), new real[] {0}); draw(thegraphs[0],blue);  draw((-9,-5)--(12,16),Arrows);  pair A,B,C,D;  B=(-2.3472,1.6528); D=(5.68053,9.68053); A=(-3.92744,4.62744); C=(0.59411,0.10589);  draw((-2.3472,-7)--(-2.3472,25),red+dashed); draw((5.68053,-7)--(5.68053,25),red+dashed);  dot(A); dot(B); dot(C); dot(D);  label(&quot;$y=x$&quot;,(-9,-2.5)); label(&quot;$y=p(x)$&quot;,(-11,18));  label(&quot;$(c,d)$&quot;,(-5.82744,4.62744)); label(&quot;$(a,a)$&quot;,(-4.4472,1.7528)); label(&quot;$(d,c)$&quot;,(0.59411,-1.10589)); label(&quot;$(b,b)$&quot;,(7.28053,8.78053));  label(&quot;$x=a$&quot;,(-4.8472,23)); label(&quot;$x=b$&quot;,(3.28053,23.2)); [/asy]\" width=\"335\" height=\"412\" />\n</p><p>Now, we show that the fixed points of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/f/36f73fc1312ee0349b3f3a0f3bd9eb5504339011.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/0/79069377f91364c2f87a64e5f9f562a091c8a6c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/e/faedb9d30dc3763d92cbcacf2cc17e2bf64f3e8b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(a,b,c,d)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"75\" height=\"20\" /> be a permutation of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/b/5/fb5b3db6f81c28ab8fbd0bd31e27292ee12c1908.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(r,1,\\tfrac{5}{2r},5)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -7px\" width=\"83\" height=\"23\" />, and suppose that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/a/1/6a1dd96466f7102cc9153ab0f570272cd1bb32d4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p(a)=a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"69\" height=\"20\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/0/3/2036f9548f533e08b6c12b3858e3ec81bb23bf4d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p(b)=b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"65\" height=\"20\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/2/c32a2f8e62b6968fc810bc37180d17db21dba9c2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p(c)=d$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"67\" height=\"20\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/a/a/0aaabccbc28dac98458e8bd398c10aed1d1c125e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p(d)=c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"67\" height=\"20\" />. WLOG, suppose <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/1/0/710e3e4f18d7c0270ab719a00adc61fa12363b1e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a&lt;b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"43\" height=\"15\" />. We first note that a point on <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/d/1/3d1db541df4771c9ef32bf4a78b920414c112e16.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y=p(x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"66\" height=\"18\" /> lies under the line <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/4/1/741a74d86df899c10724dc2f80638f5e7f599194.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y=x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"46\" height=\"13\" /> if and only if it lies between the lines <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/7/7/e77ba6189a32e5ead2cbb44585ede2285792545c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x = a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"46\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/4/1/741720281e465fc7461c32d504f6d54c5bcaff7c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x=b$\" width=\"42\" height=\"12\" />. WLOG, suppose <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/f/8/af8d724191857f085277ef62987315421ab3f353.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a&lt;d&lt;b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"77\" height=\"15\" />. Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/7/3/e7317ef941453d6727ff46e50c4d9f1f9c0f7a8a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(d,c)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"41\" height=\"20\" /> lies under the line <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/4/1/741a74d86df899c10724dc2f80638f5e7f599194.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y=x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"46\" height=\"13\" />, we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/8/c/e8c4caf5be63fefba3acfbae78c71c7af81bdd8b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c&lt;d$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"41\" height=\"13\" />. Notice that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/e/79e31171b9eaf222673b566ed3cf773e0f0b532c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(c,d)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"41\" height=\"20\" /> cannot lie between <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/d/4/ed47ef35959c171399e8f18eed4b517223823c04.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x=a$\" width=\"44\" height=\"8\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/4/1/741720281e465fc7461c32d504f6d54c5bcaff7c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x=b$\" width=\"42\" height=\"12\" /> because exactly one of the points <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/e/79e31171b9eaf222673b566ed3cf773e0f0b532c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(c,d)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"41\" height=\"20\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/7/3/e7317ef941453d6727ff46e50c4d9f1f9c0f7a8a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(d,c)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"41\" height=\"20\" /> lies below <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/4/1/741a74d86df899c10724dc2f80638f5e7f599194.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y=x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"46\" height=\"13\" />. Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/8/c/e8c4caf5be63fefba3acfbae78c71c7af81bdd8b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c&lt;d$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"41\" height=\"13\" />, it follows that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/9/fa971feb9f612675f73d1ee0d7cbd6b321ee80bd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c&lt;a&lt;d&lt;b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"109\" height=\"15\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/5/015cc9d29c63bf332da03dbb5c0f019925f4032b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(a,b,c,d) = (1,5,r,\\tfrac{5}{2r})$\" style=\"vertical-align: -7px\" width=\"181\" height=\"23\" />. Thus, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/0/3/103853b81d1c23ca967356274c80c6ad8dbac554.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p(1)=1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"68\" height=\"20\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/9/4/5945194e20f47f2bc68e02b7596638d96e50e7da.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p(5)=5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"68\" height=\"20\" />, as desired.\n</p><p>All that is left to do is to determine the leading coefficient of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/f/36f73fc1312ee0349b3f3a0f3bd9eb5504339011.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" />, which we call <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/0/f5047d1e0cbb50ec208923a22cd517c55100fa7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" />. We now know that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/5/5/255e64bf626f4925494a77fc9d923ad6fdd5e7de.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p(x) = m(x-1)(x-5) + x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"220\" height=\"20\" />. For convenience, replace <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/5/b55ca7a0aa88ab7d58f4fc035317fdac39b17861.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/2/1/3211aeb81112cd9e09b89b7a471ffd2130a88f83.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\tfrac{5}{2r}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -7px\" width=\"19\" height=\"23\" /> by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/3/7/f37bba504894945c07a32f5496d74299a37aa51c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$s$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/d/e0d2bf360290fd61d1c1557e763f2622363b3d35.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$t$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"8\" height=\"13\" />, respectively, satisfying <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/e/f/5efeb1090957bc6f602208d5c6910fe4b9ae710d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$st=\\tfrac{5}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -7px\" width=\"52\" height=\"23\" />. We have\\begin{align*} t &amp;= ms^2 - (6m-1)s + 5m \\\\ s &amp;= mt^2 - (6m-1)t + 5m.\\end{align*}Adding these two equations gives us <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/6/a/c6a51ae3513b020305434e1e6abd4d35bbfc7f1a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6m(s+t) = m(s^2+t^2) + 10m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"241\" height=\"21\" />. Dividing through by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/0/f5047d1e0cbb50ec208923a22cd517c55100fa7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" /> and using <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/6/5/c659b3fa631bd93cd39546120617a352ce2cf9dd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$s^2+t^2 = (s+t)^2 - 2st = (s+t)^2 - 5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"298\" height=\"21\" />, we find that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/e/7cee2e937bf58567cee3d8154d54d0ce2b19c1af.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$s+t=1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"72\" height=\"15\" /> or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/9/4/b94b31e5b087057df71302dd0d83a8a48cc70c01.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$s+t=5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"72\" height=\"15\" />. Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/4/dc4be21c42b8e49832d13378861f6bad8555b125.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$t&gt;1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"42\" height=\"15\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/4/d/d4d6bcf1634ee31398a62f37f6ad5e3c86181422.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$s&gt;0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"44\" height=\"15\" />, we must have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/9/4/b94b31e5b087057df71302dd0d83a8a48cc70c01.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$s+t=5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"72\" height=\"15\" />. Then, subtracting the second centered equation from the first and rearranging gives us <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/4/4/944e30a23ce3dfaf6a0a69068bab98f17c7a0c43.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$t-s + m(t^2-s^2) = (6m-1)(t-s)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"290\" height=\"21\" />. As <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/5/fc5e66ffb59fa43840d4a56bd340b0afc20c8a77.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$s\\ne t$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"39\" height=\"17\" />, we may divide through by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/9/b/59bbcf88b5ff1c75c76e60fa282ec75d6fd05525.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$t-s$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"39\" height=\"15\" /> to obtain <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/3/a/93abb61c55f6274fcfeaa117136f90ef827e601d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1 + m(s+t) = 1+5m = 6m-1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"262\" height=\"20\" />. Finally, we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/f/3/6f3eaf8047a3f5bebfc5c43e27123a15a44d7540.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m=2$\" width=\"48\" height=\"12\" />, which gives <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/f/5/df51d5f89c1dbd449d033722639fd746f0d85c76.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p(x) = 2x^2 - 11x + 10$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"178\" height=\"21\" />. The answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/8/e28a04f31f4f00fa4b1afecad7c0438b0477853e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2(12)^2 - 11(12)+10 = \\boxed{166}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"227\" height=\"25\" />.\n</p><p>~Sedro\n</p>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017105558\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.025 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.044 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 290/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 0/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 0/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 2/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 16847/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    0.000      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:33790:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017105558 and revision id 260473. Rendering was triggered because: page-view\n -->\n</div>"}